      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to determine the length of segment \\( AE \\) such that when the square \\( ABCD \\) is folded along the lines \\( DE \\) and \\( DF \\), the sides \\( AD \\) and \\( CD \\) coincide and lie on the diagonal \\( BD \\).\n\nLet's denote the length of \\( AE \\) as \\( x \\). Since \\( AE = CF \\), it follows that \\( AF = x \\) and \\( AB = x + CF = x + x = 2x \\).\n\nWhen the square is folded, \\( AE \\) and \\( CF \\) become \\( DE \\) and \\( DF \\), respectively. We need to find the coordinates of the points \\( D, E, \\) and \\( F \\) in the first quadrant of the coordinate plane.\n\nLet \\( D = (0, 0) \\), \\( A = (1, h) \\), \\( B = (1, h+1) \\), and \\( C = (h, 1) \\). Since \\( AE = x \\), \\( E \\) is at \\( (1, x) \\). Since \\( CF = x \\), \\( F \\) is at \\( (x, 1-x) \\).\n\nWhen the square is folded, \\( AD \\) and \\( CD \\) coincide and lie on the diagonal \\( BD \\). This means that \\( AD \\) and \\( CD \\) are reflections of each other across the line \\( DE \\).\n\nThe slope of \\( DE \\) is:\n\\[\n\\text{slope of } DE = \\frac{x - 0}{1 - 0} = x\n\\]\n\nThe equation of line \\( BD \\) can be derived using the points \\( B = (1, h+1) \\) and \\( D = (0, 0) \\). The slope of \\( BD \\) is:\n\\[\n\\text{slope of } BD = \\frac{h+1 - 0}{1 - 0} = h + 1\n\\]\n\nThe equation of line \\( BD \\) is:\n\\[\ny = (h+1)x\n\\]\n\nSince \\( D \\) is the origin, the line \\( DE \\) intersects \\( BD \\) at the midpoint of \\( AD \\). The midpoint of \\( AD \\) is \\( \\left( \\frac{1+1}{2}, \\frac{h+1+h}{2} \\right) = (1, h+1) \\).\n\nThe line \\( DE \\) is a vertical line passing through \\( (x, 1-x) \\), so its equation is \\( x = x \\). The intersection point of \\( DE \\) and \\( BD \\) is the midpoint of \\( AD \\), which is \\( (1, h+1) \\).\n\nSince \\( AD \\) and \\( CD \\) coincide when folded, the midpoint of \\( AD \\) must lie on \\( BD \\). Therefore, the y-coordinate of \\( AD \\) must be equal to the y-coordinate of \\( BD \\) at the intersection point. This means:\n\\[\n1 - x = (h+1)x\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( x \\):\n\\[\n1 - x = h + 1\n\\]\n\\[\n- x = h\n\\]\n\\[\nx = h - 1\n\\]\n\nSince \\( h = AE + AF = x + x = 2x \\), we have:\n\\[\nh = 4x\n\\]\n\nSubstituting \\( h = 4x \\) into the equation \\( 1 - x = h + 1 \\):\n\\[\n1 - x = 4x + 1\n\\]\n\\[\n- x = 4x\n\\]\n\\[\n-5x = 0\n\\]\n\\[\nx = 4\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the length of segment \\( AE \\) is \\( \\sqrt{16} - 4 = 4 - 4 = 4 \\). The integer value of \\( k + m \\) is:\n\\[\nk + m = 16 + 4 = 20\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{20}\n\\]",
